{% extends "simplified-account/settings/settings-layout.njk" %}


{% set settingsPageTitle %}Your provider is changing to Adyen{% endset %}

{% block settingsContent %}
  <h1 class="govuk-heading-l">{{ settingsPageTitle }}</h1>

  <p class="govuk-body">
    <a
      class="govuk-link"
      href="https://gds.blog.gov.uk/2026/06/02/building-for-the-future-making-change-simple-on-gov-uk-pay/"
    >
      GDS has procured a payment provider to replace Stripe</a
    >. This means your payment provider is changing to Adyen. We’re doing everything we can to minimise disruption.
  </p>

  <p class="govuk-body">
    Nothing will change for paying users. You do not need to contact them or tell them anything because the change will
    be invisible for them and there is nothing they need to do.
  </p>

  <h2 class="govuk-heading-m">Payment and refund reports</h2>
  <p class="govuk-body"
    >You'll still be able to download CSV files with details fo payments and refunds, including transaction fees.</p
  >

  <p class="govuk-body"
    >The structure and labelling of the CSV files will be a little different once you switch to Adyen. For example, to
    reflect changes to how fees are structured. Because of the way GOV.UK Pay receives data from Adyen, it may take a
    few minutes from when a payment is confirmed for all the data relating to that payment to be reflected in the
    reports.</p
  >

  <p class="govuk-body"
    >If you're importing the data from the CSV files into any of your systems, you'll need to check whether any
    technical work is needed on your systems to reflect the changes. See the `Arrange any technical work needed` section
    below for details.</p
  >

  <p class="govuk-body"
    >To see what the new CSV files will look like, you can
    <a class="govuk-link" href="">download a CSV file with sample Adyen transactions</a>.</p
  >

  <h2 class="govuk-heading-m">Fees</h2>
  <p class="govuk-body"
    >Adyen's fees are similar to Stripe's but are slightly different in some areas. For example, the most common type of
    card used on GOV.UK Pay is a UK debit card. Stripe charges a flat rate of a few pence plus a percentage of the value
    of the transaction. Adyen charges a higher flat rate but the percentage is lower. However, credit card fees, Amex
    fees, non-European card fees and chargebacks (also known as disputes) are cheaper. The exact change depends on your
    service's transactions.</p
  >

  <p class="govuk-body">
    <a id="download-adyen-fee-link" class="govuk-link" href="{{ feesPath }}">
      Download information about Adyen's fees (PDF)
    </a>
  </p>

  <h2 class="govuk-heading-m">Getting ready to switch to Adyen</h2>
  <p class="govuk-body">
    All services currently using Stripe will need to move to Adyen in order to keep taking payments.
  </p>
  <p class="govuk-body">
    We will contact service admins when onboarding with Adyen opens. In the meantime, there's some steps you can take to
    prepare.
  </p>

  <h3 class="govuk-heading-s">1. Prepare to complete the onboarding form</h3>

  <p class="govuk-body">
    You'll need to complete an onboarding form for each of your services in order to switch them to Adyen.</p
  >
  <p class="govuk-body"> The onboarding form will ask for similar information to when you went live with Stripe.</p>
  <p class="govuk-body"> You will need: </p>
  <ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
    <li>your organisation’s bank details</li>
    <li>
      the name, date of birth, home address, work telephone number, and work email address of someone who has the
      authority to sign a contract on behalf of your organisation (called your ‘responsible person’)
    </li>
    <li>your organisation’s VAT number (if applicable)</li>
    <li>
      the name, home address, date of birth and work email address of the director of your service (or someone at
      director level) - this must be a different person from your ‘responsible person’
    </li>
    <li>your company registration number (if applicable)</li>
  </ul>
  <p class="govuk-body">
    You can read about
    <a class="govuk-link" href="https://www.adyen.com/en_GB/privacy-policy/compliance-obligations"
      >how Adyen processes the data collected through these checks</a
    >
    and
    <a class="govuk-link" href="https://www.adyen.com/en_GB/privacy-policy/security"
      >how Adyen keeps personal data secure</a
    >.
  </p>
  <p class="govuk-body">
    You must also add a document that verifies your organisation is a government entity. This must be a copy of one of
    the following:
  </p>
  <ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
    <li>your VAT Registration</li>
    <li>your certificate of incorporation</li>
    <li>a document from Companies House</li>
    <li>a VAT certificate from HM Revenue and Customs (HMRC)</li>
    <li>an account statement from HMRC</li>
    <li>a document from the Charity Commission</li>
    <li>a document from the Scottish Charity Regulator (OSCR)</li>
  </ul>
  <p class="govuk-body"> The address on your government entity document must not be a PO box. </p>

  <h3 class="govuk-heading-s">
    Cadets, parish councils and other organisations that cannot provide a government entity document
  </h3>

  <p class="govuk-body">
    Cadets, parish councils and other organisations that cannot provide a government entity document will need to
    produce an alternative document with some different information. A template document will be available for you to
    fill in and upload.
  </p>

  <h3 class="govuk-heading-s">2. Prepare to agree to the revised GOV.UK agreement and Adyen terms</h3>
  <p class="govuk-body">When you complete the onboarding form, you'll be asked to agree to:</p>
  <p class="govuk-body"
    >- the
    <a
      class="govuk-link"
      href="https://selfservice.payments.service.gov.uk/policy/agreement-for-crown-and-non-crown-bodies"
      >revised GOV.UK Pay agreement</a
    ></p
  >
  <p class="govuk-body"
    >- the
    <a class="govuk-link" href="https://selfservice.payments.service.gov.uk/policy/agreement-schedule-7-adyen"
      >Adyen terms and conditions</a
    ></p
  >

  <h3 class="govuk-heading-s">3. Arrange any technical work needed</h3>
  <p class="govuk-body"
    >If any of your systems are receiving data from GOV.UK Pay - either because you're importing CSV files downloading
    from the GOV.UK Pay admin tool, or receiving data through the GOV.UK Pay API - the technical team looking after the
    system may need to make changes to reflect differences in the structure of the data and timing of when it's
    received.
  </p>
  <p class="govuk-body"
    >We recommend sharing these documents with your technical team as soon as possible, so they can assess how much work
    they'll need to do:</p
  >
  <p class="govuk-body"
    >-
    <a
      class="govuk-link"
      href="https://docs.payments.service.gov.uk/switch_payment_service_provider/check_stripe_to_adyen_integration/"
      >overview of technical changes to the GOV.UK Pay API</a
    ></p
  >
  <p class="govuk-body">- <a class="govuk-link">summary of API and technical changes</a></p>
  <p class="govuk-body"
    >-
    <a class="govuk-link" href="https://docs.payments.service.gov.uk/testing_govuk_pay/#mock-card-numbers-for-adyen"
      >mock card numbers for use in Adyen testing</a
    ></p
  >

  <p class="govuk-body"
    >To request an Adyen test service, contact GOV.UK Pay support at
    <a class="govuk-link" href="mailto:govuk-pay-support@digital.cabinet-office.gov.uk"
      >govuk-pay-support@digital.cabinet-office.gov.uk</a
    ></p
  >

  <h2 class="govuk-heading-m">Questions and support</h2>
  <p class="govuk-body">
    Email
    <a class="govuk-link" href="mailto:govuk-pay-support@digital.cabinet-office.gov.uk"
      >govuk-pay-support@digital.cabinet-office.gov.uk</a
    >
    if you have questions about the change of provider.
  </p>
  <p class="govuk-body">
    Please do not contact Adyen or Stripe about the move - send any questions or comments to us.
  </p>
{% endblock %}
